Mark XX: release automation + docs

- scripts/release.py (stdlib): one command per release. Bumps the version
  across pyproject.toml + __init__.py + the suite's version assertion, runs
  the smoke suite (refuses to continue on failure), builds the wheel
  (pip wheel --no-deps), builds UMBRA.exe via PyInstaller when available
  (UMBRA.spec; prints the manual step otherwise), scans the wheel for
  secret material and ABORTS on any hit, writes dist/SHA256SUMS, updates
  the README releases block (marker-delimited), and emits
  RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md with publish steps including the never-commit-
  private-keys rule. --dry-run prints the whole plan and touches nothing.
  Subprocesses use argument lists, never a shell.
- SUPPORT.md: troubleshooting table, where every data file lives, the
  diagnostics bundle flow (what is included/redacted), opt-in crash
  reporting, the health disclaimer, and the support/refund policy aligned
  with the EULA (LICENSE).
- install-instructions.txt (repo): Windows standalone exe, source install,
  Android sideload, the first-run wizard + non-interactive setup, all
  Mark XVI-XX commands (dashboard, settings, profiles, export/import,
  update check, diagnostics), LITE/PRO summary.
- docs/index.html (storefront): 24-tool desktop agent, new DASHBOARD card,
  LITE rows for dashboard/profiles/update+diagnostics, download section
  mentions the wizard, settings, profiles and the signed update checker.
- README: Releases section (marker block for release.py) + SUPPORT link.
- Version 3.7.0.
